@begin(section)

@title(3rd Party Licenses)

dsolv is built on the shoulders of giants. Here are the licenses for the
third party software that dsolv depends on:

@begin(code)
com.djhaskin.cliff   - MIT License
com.djhaskin.nrdl    - MIT License
com.djhaskin.svers   - MIT License
alexandria           - Public Domain
cl-ppcre             - BSD 2-Clause License
fset                 - BSD 2-Clause License (includes the gmap
                       generalized mapping facility)
chipz                - BSD 3-Clause License
babel                - MIT License
dexador              - MIT License
quri                 - MIT License
cl-reexport          - MIT License
arrows               - CC0 / Public Domain
trivial-features     - MIT License
trivial-package-local-nicknames - Unlicense / Public Domain
codex                - MIT License
scriba               - MIT License
@end(code)

The documentation is built with
@link[uri="https://commondoc.github.io/codex/"](codex) and
@link[uri="https://commondoc.github.io/scriba/"](scriba), which are also
MIT-licensed, together with the rest of the common-doc ecosystem
(@c(common-doc), @c(common-html), @c(docparser), @c(pandocl), @c(parenml),
and friends).

@end(section)
